   'description': '## Objective/Goal\n\nThe influences of different degrees of plastic deformation and the annealing time on the recrystallization behavior are introduced in terms of hardness and microstructure on α-brass.\n\n## Experimental procedure\n\nTo complete the experiment following steps are required.\n\n1. **High Pressure Torsion Test:** It is used to investigate the effects of the degree of deformation toward the final recrystallized grain size.\n2. **Cold Deformation by Rolling:** In order to investigate the influence of the annealing time on the recrystallization behavior, a cold deformation method on the brass alloy was implemented, followed by an annealing heat treatment with different periods of time.\n3. **Heat Treatment:** The samples from both deformation processes were placed in the furnace at a certain temperature\n4. **Embedding:** The sample was placed inside the molds and filled with the epoxy resin that acted as the embedding agent and placed in a pressure pot.\n5. **Grinding:** The metallographic preparation is implemented to get rid of the scratches and applied different conditions for grindings.\n6. **Polishing:** The polishing step was essential to provide a clear image during the imaging\n7. **Hardness Measurement:** The last step is to measure the hardness of the materials. Vickers HV1 hardness testing machine (with 1 kg of load) is used to indent the samples.',
