   'last_modified': '2023-06-12T11:00:04.606033+00:00',
   'license': None,
   'plain_description': 'Preparation of PDMS: mix prepolymer with curing agent in a ratio of 10:1 Degas PDMS for 30 min Sieve salt into different size fractions Pour 0.9 mL PDMS into master, add salt, centrifuge at 4600 rpm, 4°C, 20 min Cure in oven (70 °C) Remove MESIF from master, squeeze in warm water bath, stir at 40 °C für 24 h, change water regulary 7.Dry MESIF and cut into 18 mm long pieces Pour PDMS into master for housing, cure for 25 in oven (70 °C) Punch 4 mm contact hole in housing lid Activate housing cage and 5 MESIF with oxygen plasma (Mica Neu, 30 seconds at 300 W and 0.2 mbar) Place MESIF in housing cage with activated sites facing each other Activate housing cage incl MESIF with housing lid in plasma activator (Mica Neu, 30 seconds at 300 W and 0.2 mbar) Place lid on housing cage with actived sites facing each other, cover with foil, glass slides, fix with clamps Place in oven (90 °C) for 30 min Cut individual eachs, repair possible leaks with PDMS, wrap with aluminium foil, autoclave',
   'state': 'active',
   'tags': [],
   'title': 'Manufacturing of MESIF chips',
   'type': 'protocol',
   'visibility': 'public'},
